      "path": "force-app",
      "default": true,
      "package": "CursorBatchFramework",
      "versionDescription": "Hardens the finish() completion callback. First, finish() now fires exactly once per job: completion is treated as a threshold crossing rather than a standing condition, so only the event batch that moves the job across Total_Workers completes it. Previously a late page event or a redelivered final event could re-satisfy the condition and re-invoke finish(), duplicating whatever it chained to. Second, a finish() that throws is now recorded on the job record instead of only a debug log: the exception is appended to Error_Message__c (preserving any existing worker error, truncated at the field limit), a clean 'Completed' is upgraded to 'Completed with Errors' (never downgrading 'Failed'), and the new status is re-mirrored to CursorBatch_Job_Parent__c.Last_Job_Status__c. The same append happens on the coordinator-failure path in CursorBatchCoordinatorFinalizer. The write-back is best-effort and can never break the platform-event transaction. CursorBatchCoordinator.invokeFinishCallback() and CursorBatchWorker.invokeFinishCallback() now return the Exception instead of void, and separate class construction from the finish() call so reflection failures stay log-only and don't falsely mark a job as errored.",
      "definitionFile": "config/project-scratch-def.json",
      "installBehaviors": {
        "newOnly": [
          "main/default/platformEventSubscriberConfigs/CursorBatchCoordinatorTriggerConfig.platformEventSubscriberConfig-meta.xml",
          "main/default/platformEventSubscriberConfigs/CursorBatchWorkerTriggerConfig.platformEventSubscriberConfig-meta.xml",
          "main/default/platformEventSubscriberConfigs/CursorBatchWorkerCompleteTriggerConfig.platformEventSubscriberConfig-meta.xml"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
